@startuml agent-start-single-caller
' cumin works - the one check before a start and the single caller of Agents.Start, with the ways around that a test refuses.
' Document: cumin-core.md, topic on the stop after the runs.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

rectangle "a request to an agent\n(at a poll, or at the end of a run)" as request
rectangle "PermitStart\n(pure function, the one check)" as check
rectangle "startAgent\n(takes the permit)" as caller
rectangle "Agents.Start\n(starts the agent)" as start
rectangle "other code of the package" as other #MistyRose

request --> check : stop request read?\nquota allows?
check --> request : StartPermit\n(granted or not)
request --> caller : the permit
caller --> start : the only call,\nonly with a granted permit

other -[#red,dashed]-> start : refused: a call, a method value,\na copy of the field Agents
other -[#red,dashed]-> caller : refused: a StartPermit literal\noutside PermitStart

note bottom of other
  A test reads the source of the package
  and fails for each red arrow.
  Other methods of Agents, a comparison
  with nil, and an assignment to the field
  stay allowed.
end note
@enduml
